Subject: [PATCH] vrend: integer GLSL types for integer attributes on every host

vrend gives an integer vertex attribute (glVertexAttribIPointer) and an integer color buffer
their integer GLSL types (ivec4/uvec4) only where GL_VENDOR is "ARM", or with
VIRGL_USE_INTEGER. Elsewhere it declares them as vec4 and reads the bits back with
floatBitsToUint/floatBitsToInt, which is undefined behaviour (upstream a861e9d, "Since the old
way works fine on other GPU, only enable this fix for ARM MALI for now. The plan is to enable
this for other GPU also with auto detection").

With the float types, a flat uvec4 from an integer attribute with the value 200 reaches the
shader as 255 or more:
- ANGLE (OpenGL ES on Vulkan; the Galaxy S24 Exynos's GLES driver): for GL_UNSIGNED_BYTE and
  GL_UNSIGNED_SHORT, not for GL_UNSIGNED_INT (also with ANGLE on a desktop Vulkan driver);
- Qualcomm's Adreno 650 GLES driver: for all three.
D2GL's text shader takes its layer (GL_UNSIGNED_SHORT x2) and flags (GL_UNSIGNED_BYTE x4) from
such attributes. With the integer types, every integer attribute reads correctly on both.

use_integer() is now true on every host; VIRGL_USE_INTEGER=0 keeps the float types (for tests).
Only the declared types of integer inputs and outputs change; no data is converted.

Written for virglrenderer e18f8c00 src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c.

---
--- a/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c
+++ b/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c
@@ -7553,16 +7553,14 @@
    return &callbacks;
 }
 
+/* Integer vertex inputs and integer color outputs get their integer GLSL types on every host
+ * (upstream: only on Arm's driver, or with VIRGL_USE_INTEGER). The float types that upstream
+ * keeps elsewhere are undefined behaviour (upstream a861e9d): with them, the shader reads integer
+ * attributes wrongly on ANGLE (8-bit and 16-bit ones) and on Qualcomm's Adreno 650 driver (also
+ * 32-bit ones). VIRGL_USE_INTEGER=0 keeps the float types, for tests. */
 static bool use_integer(void) {
-   if (getenv("VIRGL_USE_INTEGER"))
-      return true;
-
-   const char * a = (const char *) glGetString(GL_VENDOR);
-   if (!a)
-       return false;
-   if (strcmp(a, "ARM") == 0)
-      return true;
-   return false;
+   const char *value = getenv("VIRGL_USE_INTEGER");
+   return !value || strcmp(value, "0") != 0;
 }
 
 static bool vrend_use_gbm_layout_feature(UNUSED uint32_t flags)
